*HEADING
FEA1B_M3R_INTERFACE  case=ARM_MANEUVER_QS  mesh=T3_TT_FINE  eltype=C3D8I  material=AL6061_T6_CAND
M7 WP7 FEA_OPERATIONAL element-formulation closure (ODR-11/ODR-12).
Units: N, mm, MPa, tonne. Linear static. DESIGN_INDICATIVE results only.
** ELEMENT_FORMULATION: C3D8I -- incompatible-mode 8-node hex, 2x2x2 full integration, no hourglass modes, incompatible modes relieve shear locking in bending-dominated thin features (PRIMARY choice)
** MESH_SERIES: THROUGH_THICKNESS  n_xy=20 (pitch 8 mm)  kz=3
** ASSUMPTION: LINEAR_STATIC_SMALL_DISPLACEMENT (NLGEOM off; loads are milli-g level)
** ASSUMPTION: BUS_SIDE_ENCASTRE_ASSUMPTION: BC-BUS-001 bus stiffness authority is HOLD; z=0 face fully clamped = stiff-boundary design bound
** ASSUMPTION: BOLT_DISK_KINEMATIC_COUPLING_ASSUMPTION: M6/M5/M4 joints modelled as rigid coupling disks (r_b=12/10/10 mm, auto-grow to >=1 node/face, recorded); no preload, no friction, no slip
** ASSUMPTION: ARM_BASE_RIGID_SPIDER_ASSUMPTION: B601 base flange stiffness >> 8 mm ring; single RP spider onto 4 as-built M4 disks; sensitivity covered by the 3-level mesh convergence series (CDR rigid_spider rule)
** ASSUMPTION: NO_CONTACT_NO_PRELOAD_NO_FRICTION: CDR joint mechanics HOLD; faces outside bolt disks untied (separation/interpenetration possible; Level-1 bound)
** ASSUMPTION: STAGE_B_IDEALIZED_ANNULAR_PLATE: pocket/recess not resolved; bore dia100 through bottom 2 layers; centre web r<50 modelled 4.0 mm (real 5.595)
** ASSUMPTION: STAGE_A_IDEALIZED_UNIFORM_RING: OD150/ID40 x 8.0 uniform; spigot, recess, counterbores not resolved
** ASSUMPTION: BRIDGE_CORNER_RADIUS_OMITTED: R4 corners modelled square; all boundaries stepped at element corners
** ASSUMPTION: SMALL_HOLES_NOT_CUT: dia6.6/5.5/4.6 holes represented by coupling disks, not voids (locally stiffer); hole-edge peak stress NOT qualified here
** ASSUMPTION: POISSON_ASSUMPTION: nu=0.33 for both Al candidates (not in M6 library)
** ASSUMPTION: MATERIALS_CANDIDATE: 6061-T6 / 7075-T651 elastic constants from M6 WP4 library, classification PROTOTYPE_CANDIDATE; margins DESIGN_INDICATIVE only
** ASSUMPTION: DYNAMIC_FACTOR_ASSUMPTION: quasi-static equivalence F_eq=DAF*J/dt, DAF=2.0, dt=0.1 s; both declared assumptions, research-bound
** ASSUMPTION: LOAD_DIRECTION_ASSUMPTION: transverse +y force plus bending moment about +z; worst-axis alignment declared (near-axisymmetric stack)
** ASSUMPTION: MEMORY_GATE_MESH_ADAPTATION: seeds 16/10/8 mm replace draft 4/2/1 mm; <=4000 C3D8R; 6.7 mm ligament NOT resolved with 3 elements; convergence assessed on global maxima trend only
** ASSUMPTION: ARM_LOADS_BOUNDED_BY_ASSUMPTION: quintic peak accel from LC-010 trajectory x r_eff=0.7 m; e-stop = 2x maneuver; arm inertia tensor not reduced (arm cases shown to be non-governing)
** ASSUMPTION: ELEMENT_FORMULATION_CHANGE: C3D8R (1 IP + hourglass control) replaced by C3D8I (2x2x2 full integration + incompatible modes). No hourglass modes exist in C3D8I, so ALLAE must collapse to ~0; this is the acceptance test
** ASSUMPTION: IP_COUNT_COMPARABILITY: C3D8R reports 1 centroidal integration point, so its 'peak von Mises' is already an element-average; C3D8I reports 8 Gauss points, whose peak is systematically above the element average in a bending field. C3D8R peak must therefore be compared against the C3D8I ELEMENT-AVERAGED value, not against the C3D8I peak IP value
** ASSUMPTION: THROUGH_THICKNESS_REFINEMENT: kz multiplies the layer count of every z segment (bridge 2kz, stage B annulus 2kz, stage B web 1kz, stage A 2kz); kz=1 reproduces the FEA-1 plane list node-for-node
** ASSUMPTION: STAIRCASE_BOUNDARY_SINGULARITY: the dia-40 / dia-100 / OD-150 circular boundaries are stepped at element corners, so each in-plane refinement level presents a DIFFERENT discrete re-entrant-corner set. Peak stress at those steps cannot converge by construction and is excluded from the region-stress convergence metric (fixed 10 mm geometric band)
** ASSUMPTION: POINT_COUPLING_SINGULARITY: the arm-base RP kinematic coupling and the per-bolt kinematic couplings are point/patch constraints; peak stress in their immediate neighbourhood rises monotonically with refinement as a constraint singularity and is reported separately (ODR-11 singularity rule), with a fixed 15 mm exclusion radius for the far-field metric
** Case load: F_y=0.31050820236037147 N, M_z=217.35574165226001 N*mm (m_arm*(quintic q2_acc_max*r_eff); M=F*r_eff)
**
